Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world's most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver-The World's Most Experienced Driver™-to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.

&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;
You will: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Define and drive the global architectural roadmap for Waymo's Data Lake, governing the transition from ad-hoc processing to a production-grade, highly scalable analytical ecosystem. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Serve as the ultimate Tech Lead (TL) over cross-domain data pipelines, governing dependencies and maintaining platform consistency across both centralized infrastructure and embedded product domains. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Champion and enforce linear DAG architectures and modern Lakehouse/Medallion standards to untangle highly coupled, opaque "spaghetti" lineage. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Chair centralized Data Design Review forums, establishing unified standards for modularized code, testing suite enforcement, DAG dependency registration, and environmentalization. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Architect common, self-service frameworks and "Managed Pipeline Services" (like hardened wrappers and templates) for downstream consumption by Data Engineers and Product Data Scientists. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Oversee core integration strategies for Data Governance, ensuring privacy (GDPR), access Control (IAM/RBAC), and pipeline compliance are deeply baked into core architecture. &nbsp; &nbsp;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;
You have: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;BS/MS/PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or equivalent. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;12+ years of experience leading the design, implementation, and operations of multi-Petabyte Data Lake/Data Warehouse solutions in high-growth companies. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Proven track record of being the Lead Architect driving significant data governance and data platform maturity transitions (e.g., ad-hoc ➔ standardized). &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Deep experience driving a data infrastructure org through rapid growing phrase, effectively balancing speed for analysts with central governance guardrails. &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Expert-level technical depth in distributed batch/streaming frameworks (e.g., C++, Flume, Apache Spark, Flink). &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Highly effective cross-functional influencer; capable of driving alignment across hundreds of Stakeholders (Director+ levels, Embedded Eng, Data Science). &nbsp; &nbsp;
&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;
We prefer: &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Hands-on knowledge of cloud-native or internal release hardening ecosystems (e.g., Canary/CAS, CI/CD pipelines, container orchestration). &nbsp; &nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;High proficiency with Google-internal pipeline/data stacks (Flume, SQLP, Rapid, CAS, F1). &nbsp; &nbsp;
